                  This is the most quantifiable H9 boundary."
        classification:  "REQUIRES_DOMAIN_KNOWLEDGE"
      }
    }
    capability_matrix_incomplete: "T4/T5 data pending human rating"
  }

// ─── KEY FINDINGS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  findings = [

    "FINDING_1: H6 is architecturally CLOSED (not just statistically resolved).
     The split grammar (computed/interpreted) makes fidelity_computed=1.0 a design invariant,
     not a model capability outcome. Ashby's Law of Requisite Variety applied at the grammar level.",

    "FINDING_2: 18× compression (450B vs 8000B) is achieved by removing computed fields
     from LLM scope. The prompt reduction is structural — no LLM tuning needed.",

    "FINDING_3: The capability boundary for VSF-domain content is MODEL-KNOWLEDGE-DEPENDENT.
     Domain misclassification (covenant→legal contract) is not a task-type failure but a
     training-data gap. The same 7b model with VSF context would likely classify correctly.
     This distinguishes two types of H9 taxonomy:
       (a) Task-type boundary (counting: computed; semantics: interpreted) — robust
       (b) Domain boundary (VSF terminology: 1.5b fails) — model-specific",

    "FINDING_4: The computed/interpreted split is PRODUCTION-READY for all computed fields.
     Interpreted fields at 1.5b quality are diagnostic-only (not operationally viable for
     mission-critical briefs). This defines the deployment threshold for EXP-PHI-02 architecture.",

    "FINDING_5: The S4 governance cycle (nucleus) operates at similar latency constraints.
     Even with phi_down s4_interval=1800s, Ollama on CPU is capacity-constrained.
     This supports the Ollama-on-LXC-110 isolation (DEBT_S4_ISOLATION) as a necessary separation.",
  ]

